dispatch/observe and WF-14's reconcile), so twenty sites have a neighbour that can answer for
them. The mechanism -- site keys, the table reconciled both ways, killed only by the named test,
never by any non-zero exit -- is `tools/site_sweep.py`, shared with the skill and pi sweeps. The
table was written from `--discover` (2026-09-26): each site's most direct case among the tests its
neuter fails, never the vocabulary census or the CLI exit case, which notice any vanished code.
Where one case serves three sites (observe's and reconcile's `malformed_reply`), it holds one input
per site and asserts the detail only that site produces (F140).

